# 📱 UI/UX Best Practices

## Design Principles

- **Consistency**: Maintain visual and interaction consistency across all screens
- **Hierarchy**: Establish clear visual hierarchy using typography, spacing, and color
- **Clarity**: Make UI elements and their purposes immediately clear to users
- **Feedback**: Provide immediate feedback for all user interactions
- **Accessibility**: Design for all users including those with disabilities

## Visual Hierarchy & Typography

- REQUIRED: Use typography scale from design system (`theme.typography.fontSizes`)
- MUST establish clear information hierarchy: Primary → Secondary → Tertiary
- REQUIRED: Maintain consistent line heights and spacing
- FORBIDDEN: More than 3 font sizes per screen
- MUST use appropriate font weights for emphasis

## Color & Contrast Standards

- REQUIRED: Meet WCAG 2.1 AA contrast requirements (4.5:1 for normal text)
- MUST use semantic colors from theme (`theme.colors.status.success`)
- FORBIDDEN: Using color alone to convey information — always include text/icons
- REQUIRED: Test with colorblind accessibility in mind

## Interactive Elements

- MUST provide clear affordances (buttons must look clickable)
- REQUIRED: Minimum touch target size of **44px (iOS)** / **48dp (Android)**
- MUST show pressed/active states for all interactive elements
- REQUIRED: Consistent interaction patterns across similar elements
- FORBIDDEN: Interactions that don't provide immediate feedback

## Loading States

- MUST implement skeleton loaders for all async operations
- REQUIRED: Use design system `<Skeleton>` components
- FORBIDDEN: Blank screens during loading
- REQUIRED: Progressive loading for complex interfaces
- MUST show loading progress for operations >2 seconds

## Empty States

- MUST provide helpful empty states for all lists and data-driven screens
- REQUIRED: Use `<EmptyState>` component with actionable guidance
- MUST include relevant action buttons
- REQUIRED: Contextual illustration or icon
- MUST explain what the empty state means and how to resolve it

## Error Handling & Messaging

- MUST implement consistent error handling
- REQUIRED: Use toast notifications for user feedback
- MUST provide recovery actions where possible
- REQUIRED: Clear, human-readable error messages
- FORBIDDEN: Technical error messages shown to users (no stack traces, error codes, etc.)
- MUST validate forms in real-time with helpful guidance

## Form Design Standards

- REQUIRED: Clear field labels above or inside inputs
- MUST provide helper text for complex fields
- REQUIRED: Real-time validation with constructive error messages
- MUST group related fields logically
- REQUIRED: Clear primary vs secondary actions
- FORBIDDEN: More than 7 fields visible at once without grouping

## Form Component Priority

### Priority 1: FormField Component (MANDATORY for new forms)

```typescript
// ✅ REQUIRED PATTERN for all new forms
<FormField
  label="Email"
  value={value}
  onChangeText={onChange}
  error={error?.message}
  helperText="Optional guidance"
/>
```

### Priority 2: Shared Form Utilities (for existing/legacy forms)

```typescript
import {
  createSharedFormStyles,
  getInputStyle,
  getInputVariant,
} from "@design-system/utils";

const sharedStyles = createSharedFormStyles(theme);

<Input
  variant={getInputVariant(error, success)}
  style={getInputStyle(sharedStyles, error, success)}
/>;
```

### Legacy Pattern (Being Phased Out)

- **DEPRECATED**: Manual `input` + `inputError` styles in component files
- **MIGRATION REQUIRED**: Move to `FormField` or shared utilities
- **FORBIDDEN**: New forms with duplicated style definitions

## Navigation & Information Architecture

- MUST maintain consistent navigation patterns
- REQUIRED: Clear page/screen titles and context
- MUST provide back navigation for all deep flows
- REQUIRED: Bottom navigation for primary app sections
- FORBIDDEN: More than 5 primary navigation items

## Responsive & Adaptive Design

- REQUIRED: Design works on all device sizes (phone, tablet)
- MUST use flexible layouts with proper constraints
- REQUIRED: Appropriate spacing for different screen densities
- MUST consider landscape orientation where applicable
- REQUIRED: Safe area handling for all devices with notches

## Animation & Micro-interactions

- MUST use subtle animations to guide attention
- REQUIRED: Loading animations for state changes
- FORBIDDEN: Feedback animations longer than 300ms
- MUST provide reduced motion alternatives
- REQUIRED: Consistent easing and timing across animations

## Accessibility (a11y) Standards

- REQUIRED: Screen reader compatibility with proper `accessibilityLabel` on all interactive elements
- MUST provide `accessibilityLabel` / `alt` for all images and icons
- REQUIRED: Keyboard navigation support where applicable
- MUST maintain focus indicators for navigation
- REQUIRED: Sufficient color contrast ratios (WCAG 2.1 AA)
- FORBIDDEN: Auto-playing media without user control

## UI/UX Prohibitions

- **NO** touch targets smaller than 44px (iOS) / 48dp (Android)
- **NO** color-only information — always pair with text or icon
- **NO** auto-playing media without user control
- **NO** feedback animations longer than 300ms
- **NO** technical error messages shown to users
- **NO** forms with more than 7 fields without proper grouping
- **NO** color contrast below WCAG 2.1 AA standards
- **NO** missing focus indicators for keyboard navigation
- **NO** inconsistent interaction patterns within the same feature
- **NO** missing `accessibilityLabel` for images and icons
- **NO** new forms using manual `Controller + Input` patterns (use `FormField`)
- **NO** duplicating form styles across components
